# ~/.claude — DENYLIST. Managed by home/srvs/claude-state.nix; edits here are
# overwritten on the next sync. Change the nix source instead.
#
# This repo deliberately carries the WHOLE ~/.claude tree, session transcripts
# included: the user wants a session started on `top` to be readable on `book`.
# That is the opposite of the allowlist this file used to be, so the rule that
# keeps it safe is different. An allowlist could not widen by accident; a
# denylist can. What follows is therefore organised around two questions —
# is it a SECRET, and is it MACHINE-LOCAL — and nothing else is excluded.
#
# The remote is PRIVATE. Treat everything in it as internal documents: it holds
# verbatim transcripts of whatever was on screen during every session.

# ---- secrets: never, under any circumstances --------------------------------
# .credentials.json is a live OAuth token; daemon/control.key authenticates to
# the local daemon. The wildcards exist because a future Claude Code release can
# add a secret file we have not heard of, and a denylist only protects what it
# names. Keep them broad.
.credentials.json
*credential*
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
*token*

# .claude.json backups — rotated every few minutes AND copies of a file that has
# held auth material. Either reason alone disqualifies them.
backups/

# ---- machine-local runtime state --------------------------------------------
# Live process state, not documents. Syncing these is not merely wasteful: the
# daemon keeps a warm pool of pre-spawned background sessions, and job dirs are
# LIVE PROCESSES on the machine that owns them. Landing `top`'s job dirs on
# `book` invites its daemon to adopt sessions whose processes do not exist.
jobs/
daemon/
sessions/
session-env/
tasks/
.trash-claude-sessions/

# Shell snapshots capture this machine's PATH and functions — NixOS store paths
# are meaningless on Fedora Asahi, and vice versa.
shell-snapshots/

# Caches: re-fetched or regenerated on demand, and churning on every invocation.
cache/
paste-cache/
downloads/
telemetry/
plugins/cache/
plugins/marketplaces/
plugins/plugin-catalog-cache.json
*-cache.json
.last-*
*.log
*.lock

# ---- kept on purpose (do not "clean up") ------------------------------------
# projects/**        session transcripts + memory files — the point of this repo
# file-history/      per-session edit history
# plans/             written plans
# orchestrator-briefing.md, and any other top-level doc
# history.jsonl      prompt history (merge=union, see .gitattributes)
# settings.json, plugins/installed_plugins.json, plugins/known_marketplaces.json
